# Roth IRA / TVM Retirement Model

Rebuild of an Excel actuarial/finance model as a web app (portfolio piece, exam FM material). Reimplement logic cleanly in Python — do not port spreadsheet cell mechanics.

## Stack

- Backend: Python FastAPI + Pydantic; single `POST /api/calculate`
- Frontend: vanilla HTML/CSS/JS (no bundler); Chart.js via CDN
- Flow: form change → debounce ~300ms → full recalculate → re-render charts/tables from fresh JSON

## Layout

```
backend/   app.py, models.py, engine.py, tax.py, actuary.py, scenarios.py, tests/
frontend/  index.html, style.css, app.js
```

Handoff source of truth: `Cursor_WebApp_Handoff (1).md`

## Build order (section 11)

1. Backend core (engines, IRA limits, base tax)
2. Filing status + state tax + transition
3. Actuary Mode + salary cap
4. Growth Multiple / Terminal Value by vintage (include seed)
5. Milestones
6. What-If scenarios + required-return solver
7. Frontend + Chart.js + design system
8. QA against handoff section 9

Prioritize correct math over UI polish. Never invent Excel expected values — use fixtures Steven provides.

## `init` command

On literal user message `init` only: greet with status (handoff confirmed, one-line project summary, build-order checklist with progress, ask phase + Excel I/O pairs). Do not auto-start coding. Normal messages get normal responses — no checklist spam.
